    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n327" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγᾰνάκτ-ησις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>physical pain and irritation,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. περὶ τὰ οὖλα,</span> of the
			irritation caused by teething, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				251c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>vexation,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγανάκτησιν ἔχει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.41
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>2 Ep.Cor.</u>
				7.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				4.4.19
			</span></i>:—of God, <i>wrath,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Marc.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Gal.</u>
				171e
			</span></i>.</div>
